00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.210
So first thing, I'll just quickly talk about our infrastructure.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.520
We have a few different tools that we're going to use during this course, and

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.490
we are hosting all these applications ourselves on our own hardware,

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.860
which is currently at the new Fab Hub in Kendall, Boston.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.755
So we're very proud of this because we control the data, we're private, and then

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:57.435
we can make sure that this documentation lives on as long as possible so that your

00:00:57.481 --> 00:01:02.071
work can be shared for multiple generations, we hope.

00:01:04.321 --> 00:01:05.430
So the

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.755
first big platform is the FabLabs.io. It's for the network.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:13.620
It's listing all our Fab Labs around the world.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:20.220
It's been around for a long time. And this is a great place to find other

00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:25.980
labs as well. And we use this also as a login system because you can have

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.080
accounts on here, and these accounts can be logged into other platforms that want

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.330
to share with the Fab Lab network. So we're using this sort of single sign-on entry

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.080
point. So in a lot of places, when you log into our

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.540
applications, you'll be going through the FabLabs.io platform.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.880
You can also visit it to find other labs, and there's also a forum with a wider

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.211
network if you want to go there.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.101
The other big platform, which you'll be using a lot for your documentation, is the

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:07.980
GitLab platform we call. It's a hosted Git repository, so this allows-- Git is a

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:13.665
version control system that basically keeps track of all your changes to your

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.195
website, and then it provides a web interface so that you can do everything through

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.730
the browser, interact with your website.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.160
It also has a code editor, so you can do all your coding within a browser window

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:26.730
and

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.980
also interact with it from your computer, and it's just a big collaboration

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.090
platform, and we're using it to host all your websites together.

00:02:36.825 --> 00:02:41.115
And then this GitLab platform is also automatically building your website every

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.391
time you make changes to it. It's building your website and publishing it.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.280
So it's a big tool. We're using a small part of it, and I'll go over it in a bit.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.750
The next one is Nouval. This is our evaluation program that we built specifically

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.205
for the Academy programs,

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:05.851
and this allows students and instructors to keep track of each week's

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:11.370
work and make comments, and so that you can--

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:17.190
sort of a central place for all your assessment evaluations.

00:03:19.531 --> 00:03:23.070
And then we have Matamos, which you might have already tried to log into.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:29.070
This is our chat platform. It's a very large software that is used a

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:34.291
lot in security environments, but they have an open source version, which we took

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.270
on very early on in its development and we're still using today, and which just

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:43.875
basically allows us to have multiple channels and everyone can talk to each other.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:49.140
We get notifications, and there's a phone app, and so this is just our personal

00:03:49.201 --> 00:03:52.770
platform that we can use to communicate with each other.

