00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.510
So what are we doing? What about your website? How does this all work?

00:07:56.730 --> 00:08:01.651
So for documenting your work, we're providing you a ready-made template with

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.540
everything you need to get started.

00:08:04.561 --> 00:08:10.395
And we'll be using a language called

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.865
Markdown that will automatically-- So it's a bit easier to understand Markdown, and

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.081
it will convert this into HTML, which is used to make your website.

00:08:19.561 --> 00:08:22.380
We'll be using a tool called Zenskie.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.651
I'll talk about it next slide. And

00:08:27.151 --> 00:08:29.355
yeah. If you don't know,

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:36.331
HTML code is everything that your browser is reading to build your website.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:40.591
So everything your browser is communicating with through the servers around the

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.790
world, they read HTML. So this looks like on the right.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:51.030
It's basically a markup language that just describes how to display the content.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:51.345
So it's

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:57.151
just looking at the image on the right, you say have a title of the page, then you

00:08:57.181 --> 00:09:02.520
have a body where the content is. H1 is like the heading, the first heading, and P

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.760
is for paragraph. So you have all these kinds of syntax that describe what the

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:10.554
content is. And then the browser reads this HTML and decides how to display it.

00:09:10.974 --> 00:09:13.914
The browser is the one that decides how it looks like.

00:09:14.694 --> 00:09:20.034
And then we also have a language called CSS as a cascade style sheet,

00:09:20.664 --> 00:09:21.804
which is used to

00:09:23.814 --> 00:09:25.795
adjust the style that the browser makes.

00:09:25.854 --> 00:09:31.733
So, the browser might decide an H1 has got 10 pixels font

00:09:31.795 --> 00:09:35.513
size, and they say, "Well, I don't like that," and they use CSS to change that.

00:09:36.264 --> 00:09:40.045
So these are the layers. You start with HTML. The CSS is sort of the styling.

00:09:41.694 --> 00:09:46.464
So if you would like to go into the HTML, there's a

00:09:46.674 --> 00:09:49.734
w3schools.com has a great sort of a tutorial.

00:09:50.484 --> 00:09:55.658
I would have a quick play there, just go through there, just at least read it like

00:09:55.705 --> 00:10:00.474
a book, just get familiar with all the different elements, so that later on in

00:10:00.504 --> 00:10:05.455
working with your website, when you see these things, they won't look so foreign.

00:10:07.045 --> 00:10:11.184
And the more you do that, the more you sort of understand what each of these, like

00:10:11.214 --> 00:10:15.564
a P tag is a paragraph. Then it starts to become intuitive, and it won't become

00:10:15.624 --> 00:10:21.205
scary. And then you'll sort of get excited because there'll be a new error message

00:10:21.264 --> 00:10:26.334
or a new thing that doesn't work, and you will get sort of an adrenaline rush by

00:10:26.424 --> 00:10:29.545
figuring it out and getting on to the next error message.

00:10:30.534 --> 00:10:34.674
So yeah, really enjoy the experimenting and learn to build your own website,

00:10:35.545 --> 00:10:40.614
because it's fun when you can start making your own things the way you want as you

00:10:40.644 --> 00:10:42.474
envision them. It's going to be a lot of fun.

00:10:44.214 --> 00:10:49.974
So we're not going to ask you to make-- making all your HTML is a lot of work when

00:10:50.034 --> 00:10:53.484
you're writing text, and your documentation, and your notes.

00:10:53.634 --> 00:10:58.433
So we're using a language called Markdown, which is a very simplified

00:10:59.634 --> 00:11:02.064
way of just telling text what it looks like.

00:11:02.184 --> 00:11:07.614
So this is just a plain text way of saying, okay, these are paragraphs, these are

00:11:08.154 --> 00:11:12.580
titles. So if you see like there's a hash, it's like a title, and then it sort of

00:11:12.594 --> 00:11:16.884
converts it to, this is what it would interpret those things as.

00:11:17.799 --> 00:11:17.799
So,

00:11:19.464 --> 00:11:25.314
for example, you have these code little symbols that you put in front of the words

00:11:25.344 --> 00:11:28.014
that tell it, okay, this is a title, this is a subtitle.

00:11:28.825 --> 00:11:31.404
Then we have italics.

00:11:34.494 --> 00:11:39.354
With asterisks, you can say, "This text is italics," and, "This text is bold." So

00:11:39.804 --> 00:11:45.684
it's not quite like using a word editor, but it allows you to, with very little

00:11:47.664 --> 00:11:51.024
characters, describe what your content is and how to display it.

00:11:51.714 --> 00:11:54.295
So you have on the middle column, we have here lists.

00:11:54.325 --> 00:11:56.814
So this is how you would show a list and a sub-bullet point.

00:11:58.374 --> 00:12:02.814
Images, we have this sort of like exclamation mark and square and round brackets.

00:12:03.054 --> 00:12:08.575
This is going to be very important later, and I'll show you a bit, just

00:12:08.784 --> 00:12:11.394
a quick overview of what Markdown looks like.

00:12:11.455 --> 00:12:11.814
And

00:12:17.064 --> 00:12:22.658
then the final piece of the puzzle is to get the whole Markdown and HTML to work

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:25.404
together and to have something that you can publish as a website.

00:12:25.464 --> 00:12:27.144
We're using a tool called Zentangle.

00:12:28.795 --> 00:12:34.719
Now, this is a nice tool that someone built in the community.

00:12:34.748 --> 00:12:39.939
It's an open source tool that's basically converting Markdown into HTML and then

00:12:40.014 --> 00:12:42.864
making their own opinionated style.

00:12:42.924 --> 00:12:44.828
So as you see on the right, this is

00:12:46.075 --> 00:12:50.890
what it looks like out of the box, and it's good for documentation because

00:12:51.624 --> 00:12:54.894
everything's in a uniform and there's a lot of features that's geared towards

00:12:54.908 --> 00:12:58.974
documenting. This tool is geared towards documenting.

00:12:59.124 --> 00:13:02.408
And so in the very basic form, it's just Markdown, HTML, but there's a lot of

00:13:02.454 --> 00:13:07.374
little options you can turn on and different features, and so there's a lot to look

00:13:07.464 --> 00:13:10.884
into, and we'll play around with it a bit later.

